{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787076421261668804,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bacciform-vain-canvasback","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c2b9a8d58911da59609cd16a613a49fcb86ad85c3301dc9a8ea74adf0d56430c","event_uuid":"a4f24561-2173-4ca6-b0f9-21d73efb8e74","position":{"commit_sha":"ec8ac349f864a3aef13b3e913783b33d25e9a087","position":"1787069577075394001-a4f24561-2173-4ca6-b0f9-21d73efb8e74"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d7cecb31ffe8117514fcd5dab7f44b84f0d7a2a11ce9213ba693cff5da06143a","event_uuid":"4254d57d-3805-4704-b0c1-08a6c1a9f4b4","position":{"commit_sha":"a042ee2681f5f66b967f7fd2ae6d2078d292f8d4","position":"1787069731722828001-4254d57d-3805-4704-b0c1-08a6c1a9f4b4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5431cd7d31585153d87dd01daf1007b5a77f14903984ab942f4a9aefa9935127","event_uuid":"eaf36253-0a1f-4e1d-9b61-05c5e34be36d","position":{"commit_sha":"b9dc5ee01a71ab30c49662b2811e73958f7547e7","position":"1787069739663833001-eaf36253-0a1f-4e1d-9b61-05c5e34be36d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7df357307ce6b4a46305ba3dfb3e592b35e3fb2207ffb9cde6b5c83d645f9271","event_uuid":"bd9ec12b-f5b9-4f1c-b6c5-78caed545cc2","position":{"commit_sha":"5bcbcdad9aa443c9659b0a6612f275c3865b9391","position":"1787069881807142001-bd9ec12b-f5b9-4f1c-b6c5-78caed545cc2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"34e24f8a7b156f102e654a1500bdd4549500f435ef0b36fd73b685d923ae0e71","event_uuid":"ded2ca48-1e24-4759-aa88-c14ddecbb214","position":{"commit_sha":"6de30cbdcb3892a66b62595198e0a988186b9bc7","position":"1787070720600931001-ded2ca48-1e24-4759-aa88-c14ddecbb214"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787069577075394001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bd9ec12b-f5b9-4f1c-b6c5-78caed545cc2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S2, command identity/help and every handler grammar come from the registry/parser system, but real execution still traverses explicit intercept/dispatch ladders and policy frozensets. Leaving those selection authorities in parallel preserves the coordination defect RP-05 is intended to remove.\n\n## Approach\nMove core top-level execution to the selected registry route after the pre-operation help boundary. Resolve only the selected lazy handler reference and invoke it through a closed typed adapter-kind set matching existing call shapes. The router passes the original command remainder unchanged; the selected handler uses S2's shared argparse factory. The router must not parse command/nested options a second time.\n\nConsume route metadata for:\n\n- central best-effort mount eligibility;\n- strict initialization `none`, `init_only`, or `full`, plus narrow pure selectors for genuinely conditional cases;\n- position-independent confirmation/output extraction while preserving tokens after `--`;\n- legacy output passthrough for `create`, `idea`, `transition`, `claim`, and `reopen`;\n- exact handler adapter, argv, stdout/stderr, exit-code, and exception contracts.\n\nBefore cutover, compare registry-derived policies and selected handler/parser pairs to every existing set and arm. Any non-allowlisted delta fails shadow parity. Cut over one selection authority only after parity is exact; keep derived compatibility exports for S6 rollback.\n\nThis story covers core and bridge execution that does not change optional-capability posture. S4 owns selected optional mode/backend checks and may proceed from the same S2 contract without editing dispatch.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nThe positive rationale is a single validated selection/dispatch authority while preserving specialized parser-backed handlers. No signature introspection, middleware pipeline, eager parser-tree construction, or second parse is added. Rollback selects the derived compatibility exports; no event, ticket, bridge, or binding data changes.\n\n## Testing\nUse real CLI subprocess contracts rather than source greps. Extend mount/init, mutation confirmation, global output, bridge vocabulary, hidden alias, unknown, and exit-code suites. Add typed fake handlers for every adapter kind/selector. Include negative controls for tokens after `--`, malformed global flags, no-auto-mount commands, store-touching intercepts, handler exceptions, and a parser spy proving the selected handler parses exactly once while unrelated factories/handlers are not imported.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every core canonical command and compatibility spelling resolves exactly one lazy handler through a closed adapter kind, and only the selected handler/parser modules are imported.\n- [ ] The top-level router preserves original remainder argv and the selected S2 factory parses it exactly once; no route-level option grammar exists.\n- [ ] Registry-derived mount/init behavior matches the pre-cutover census for every route, including no-auto-mount and conditional cases.\n- [ ] Confirmation, global output extraction, legacy JSON shapes, `--`, streams, exit codes, and exception propagation match existing behavioral tests.\n- [ ] Bridge compatibility spellings and hidden `bridge-status` execute through approved adapters while `purge-bridge` remains unknown.\n- [ ] Execution can switch back to derived compatibility exports without handler, generated-help, or persisted-data changes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"Replace execution ladder with selected lazy route dispatch."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"Closed invocation adapter kinds and execution policy metadata."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py","reason":"New handler/selector/adapter dispatch tests."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"Real route, argv, stream, and exit behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py","reason":"Best-effort mount and no-auto-mount behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py","reason":"Global output and tokens-after-double-dash contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_leaf_writes_parity.py","reason":"Confirmation and legacy output parity."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py","reason":"Canonical and compatibility bridge dispatch."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"],["parent","09ae-e827-1cac-452d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"e499-704e-fa13-4916","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S3 — Dispatch core CLI execution through validated lazy routes","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_cli_registry_dispatch.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_space_form_options.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_leaf_writes_parity.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC3","dd_text":"Lazy route dispatch, mount/init, argv, output, and errors"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","dd_id":"AC4-AC5","dd_text":"Bridge/retired vocabulary and compatibility rollback parity"}]},"source_event_uuids":["a4f24561-2173-4ca6-b0f9-21d73efb8e74","4254d57d-3805-4704-b0c1-08a6c1a9f4b4","eaf36253-0a1f-4e1d-9b61-05c5e34be36d","bd9ec12b-f5b9-4f1c-b6c5-78caed545cc2","ded2ca48-1e24-4759-aa88-c14ddecbb214"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787076421261668804,"uuid":"cb9cebc1-3adf-40b4-b6c0-fc2f247c44f7"}